     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for an adult. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use. At that dose the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events is high, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nThe order may have a typo or a mix-up between the per-dose and daily amounts. These are common standard regimens:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily:** 1,600 mg/day total.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily:** 2,400 mg/day.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily:** 2,400 mg/day. 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day) is the absolute ceiling.\n\nMedication orders also need to come from a licensed prescriber, or be confirmed by one, under hospital policy. Please ask the treating clinician to confirm the intended dose and frequency. Once I have a corrected order, I'll enter it right away."
      }
