       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day is about twice the maximum daily dose and could seriously harm the patient. A confirmation from someone who isn't the treating prescriber doesn't make the dose safe, and it doesn't satisfy the prescriber verification that orders require.\n\nHere is how we can move forward:\n- **Corrected dose:** If you tell me the intended regimen, I'll enter it. For example, 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day) or 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day).\n- **Intentional high dose:** If the treating physician really wants this dose, they should enter it themselves and document why. Pharmacy would also need to review it.\n\nDo you want me to enter one of the standard regimens?"
      }
